{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/sharpen Investigate why a command-line application sometimes loses the last line of output when it exits."}]},"session_id":"389299ca-1ff2-4972-87f0-a478391614c8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. A top systems engineer would isolate the failing exit path, distinguish application buffering from terminal/pipe capture loss, and produce a minimal deterministic reproduction.\n\n2. They would start from raw stdout/stderr bytes, syscall traces, exit status/signal data, and source code around the final write, flush, cleanup, and termination—not summarized logs.\n\n3. They would use repeated controlled runs, byte-level output comparison, pipe-versus-PTY tests, and syscall tracing (`strace`, `dtruss`, or platform equivalent), followed by targeted instrumentation and a regression test.\n\n4. Correctness would be demonstrated by a repeatable reproducer that fails before the fix, syscall or instrumentation evidence identifying the loss point, and a stress regression test that passes across the relevant output destinations and exit paths.\n\nRewritten prompt:\n\n> Investigate why this command-line application intermittently loses its final output line during exit.\n>\n> Establish a minimal reproducible case and determine exactly where the bytes are lost: before the application writes them, in user-space buffering, during cleanup or termination, at the OS write boundary, or in the process capturing/displaying output.\n>\n> Work from raw evidence:\n> - byte-for-byte captures of stdout and stderr\n> - exit codes and terminating signals\n> - syscall traces of writes and process termination\n> - source code and instrumentation around the final write, flush, cleanup, and exit paths\n>\n> Compare repeated runs under the output destinations relevant to this application, such as a terminal, pipe, redirected file, or PTY. Use the tracing and instrumentation tools appropriate to the target platform.\n>\n> Deliver:\n> - a deterministic or statistically characterized reproducer\n> - the evidence-backed root cause\n> - the smallest justified fix\n> - a regression test that fails before the fix and survives repeated stress runs afterward\n>\n> Leave the target platforms, output destinations, acceptable performance impact, and required confidence threshold for me to specify."}]},"session_id":"389299ca-1ff2-4972-87f0-a478391614c8"}
